{"parseRefreshTokenResponse overwrites missing refresh tokens with placeholder 'refresh_token' string, which will clobber valid refresh tokens downstream and break future refreshes": 0.9213511347770691, "minimumTokenResponseSchema uses [z.string().toString()] which yields a literal key and makes it required, so real token payloads will fail validation": 0.9302847981452942, "googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts stores entire parseRefreshTokenResponse wrapper object as credential key instead of extracting .data property": 0.9766381978988647, "refreshOAuthTokens returns a Response object when credential sharing is enabled but returns refreshFunction() result otherwise - callers expect .data property which doesn't exist on Response objects": 0.832763135433197, "zoho-bigin/lib/CalendarService.ts passes credentialId instead of credential.userId to refreshOAuthTokens, causing sync to target wrong subject": 0.825904369354248, "No response validation in refreshOAuthTokens - the fetch response status and content aren't checked": 0.7548258900642395, "salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts uses stale credentialKey values when creating jsforce connection instead of refreshed token values": 0.868516743183136, "appCredentialWebhookRequestBodySchema.parse can throw on invalid payload, turning bad input into 500s instead of 400s": 0.8822101354598999, "Handler accepts any HTTP method but should enforce POST with a 405 response like other webhook handlers": 0.715899646282196, "Header lookup is case-sensitive - if CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME is set in mixed case, lookup will fail because Node.js normalizes incoming headers to lowercase": 0.8418566584587097, "Header lookup doesn't handle arrays - if the header is sent multiple times, req.headers[...] will be an array and comparison against a string will incorrectly allow the request through": 0.39524564146995544, "JSON.parse(symmetricDecrypt(...)) can throw on decrypt/JSON errors, turning bad input into 500s instead of 400s": 0.8518106341362